  "report": "CHANGES REQUESTED: one narrow P2 remains in the new public fixture probe. boolean-receipt-probe.py:18-21 hashes its common-root regular archive to EOF before a compressed-size/read-count bound. Existing opened protection already rejects links/FIFOs; the finding concerns only the initial unbounded regular-file read. Apply the fixed256MiB/expected-size checks on that same FD before hashing and cap cumulative reads.\n\nORDINARY-SPEC-01 is otherwise statically repaired: both reader and exclusive creation guard require exact int. Retained real public true/1.0 RED acceptances0 become GREEN refusals1, with wrapper exits kept distinct. Before/after sources match their committed anchors, original two review reports are preserved byte-for-byte, original verifier0 and ten negative refusals are retained. The initial small-reader setup refusal remains separate from genuine acceptance REDs.\n\nIndependently streamed and hashed both separate malformed full capsules: each133177 members/258482 physical headers. Only receipts/ordinary.json differs from the original inventory, and only exitCode differs semantically (bool versus float). All other133176 members, source7931 and plan bytes match; fixed full limits are unchanged and no member exceeds64MiB. Both indexes clearly mark synthetic non-authoritative fixtures. Original archive9c8c1bcb and its native inventory/source/summary pins remain unchanged. No original133k rescan, captured/public verifier execution, Key/network call, root/worker modification, race/outer read or future17 approval occurred.",
